5204	/// `just haq-blind-review` and `scripts/haqp_fuzz_campaign.sh 1800`. That made
5205	/// `haq-verify` a second complete campaign, with a second fuzz run and a second
5206	/// pair of paid model reviews inside every lane, and it threatened §7's
5207	/// eight-hour ceiling with work that produced no new evidence.
5208	///
5209	/// It had never fired: `scope_traces` was empty, so the loop body never ran.
5210	/// Populating it — which `verify_corpus_scope_presence` requires — would have
5211	/// switched it on.
5212	///
5213	/// Ruling (Brian, 2026-09-04): the trace is evidence FROM the campaign. The
5214	/// lane captures each scope under strace as it actually runs, and the gate
5215	/// checks the recorded bytes: the command matches the closed lane registry, the
5216	/// path digest matches, no stage wrote to the repository's locked corpus and no
5217	/// carved fuzz binary touched it at all (F-44 ruling, 2026-09-05), and every
5218	/// traced corpus path resolves inside the tree. What is lost is the reproducibility claim that
5219	/// re-execution made; what is gained is evidence describing the run that
5220	/// happened rather than a different one.
